5
00:00:09,365 --> 00:00:13,965
(Penny:)It is... It's been in the news.
And it's a very famous boson.

6
00:00:15,271 --> 00:00:17,761
Nice try. No, in 1964...

7
00:00:17,974 --> 00:00:21,204
(Sheldon:)...Dr. Peter Higgs, accomplished
self-promoter and physicist...

8
00:00:21,377 --> 00:00:23,677
(Sheldon:)...he wrote a paper
postulating the existence...

9
00:00:23,846 --> 00:00:26,676
(Sheldon:)...of a subatomic particle
called the Higgs boson.

10
00:00:26,849 --> 00:00:29,439
(Sheldon:)Now, initially, the paper was rejected.

11
00:00:29,619 --> 00:00:31,709
(Sheldon:)But recently, he was proven right.

12
00:00:31,888 --> 00:00:34,758
(Sheldon:)And now he's on the fast track
to win a Nobel Prize.

13
00:00:34,924 --> 00:00:37,914
- Yeah. That's basically what I said.
- Yeah...

14
00:00:38,928 --> 00:00:43,768
(Sheldon:)The point is, Higgs is being celebrated
for work he did 50 years ago.

15
00:00:43,933 --> 00:00:45,123
(Sheldon:)So that got me thinking.

16
00:00:45,301 --> 00:00:49,931
(Sheldon:)Perhaps I've already hit upon the idea
that will win me my Nobel Prize.

17
00:00:50,106 --> 00:00:53,876
